# Storybook

**Scope:** React stories run in `apps/react`; Vue stories in `apps/vue`. Co-locate `<name>.stories.tsx` (React) or `<name>.stories.ts` (Vue) in public shared package source. React component rules: [React Component Patterns](react-component.mdc).

Reference: [Storybook Docs](https://storybook.js.org/docs).

Storybook **10**, CSF. React uses `@storybook/react-vite` (`.stories.tsx`); Vue uses `@storybook/vue3-vite` (`.stories.ts`).

## React setup

- **Preview:** `import preview from "#/storybook/preview"` — `#/storybook/*` maps to the runner’s `.storybook` (React → `apps/react/.storybook`, Vue → `apps/vue/.storybook`). Do not use `@/storybook/…`.
- **Meta:** `const meta = preview.meta({ … })` — no default export; stories via `meta.story({ … })`.
- **Global decorator:** `apps/react/.storybook/decorators/app-decorator.tsx` (theme, app `Provider`, padding). Per-story decorators only when a story needs extra context (e.g. mounting a portal host or `<Toaster />`).
- **Autodocs:** enable in `apps/react/.storybook/preview.tsx` (`tags: ["autodocs"]`) — do not disable per file.

### React imports

| What | Path |
| ---- | ---- |
| Preview | `#/storybook/preview` |
| UI components | `@pisagor/react` (light) or `@pisagor/react/<heavy>` |
| Hooks | `@pisagor/react/hooks` or `@pisagor/react-hooks` |
| Utils | `@pisagor/utils` |
| Form module under test | `@pisagor/react-form/tanstack` (hook) or `@pisagor/react-form` / relative `./<name>` (field under test) |
| Block under test | `@pisagor/react-blocks/<name>` |
| Storybook config | `apps/react/.storybook/` |
| Global decorator | `apps/react/.storybook/decorators/app-decorator.tsx` |
| Recipes | `apps/react/src/recipes/<group>/` — one `<variant>.tsx` per recipe, one `<group>.stories.tsx` |

Prefer `@pisagor/react` for light UI imports in stories (including the component under test). Heavy components (`data-grid`, `charts`, `rich-text-editor`, `phone-input`) stay on dedicated subpaths.

`@pisagor/react`, `@pisagor/react-hooks`, and `@pisagor/utils` resolve via workspace package exports (same as apps). Runner-only alias `#/storybook/*` lives in each runner’s `tsconfig.json` and each package’s `tsconfig.json`; Vite reads it via `resolve.tsconfigPaths`. Story files are type-checked by the runner and the owning package `tsconfig.json`:

| Consumer | Extends |
| -------- | ------- |
| `packages/react`, `packages/react-form`, `packages/react-blocks` | [`@pisagor/tsconfig/react-stories`](../../../packages/tsconfig/react-stories/tsconfig.json) |
| `apps/react` | [`@pisagor/tsconfig/react-vite`](../../../packages/tsconfig/react-vite/tsconfig.json) |
| `packages/vue` | [`@pisagor/tsconfig/vue-stories`](../../../packages/tsconfig/vue-stories/tsconfig.json) |
| `apps/vue` | [`@pisagor/tsconfig/vue-vite`](../../../packages/tsconfig/vue-vite/tsconfig.json) |

## Vue setup

- Stories: CSF via `preview.meta` + `meta.story` (`.stories.ts`), same as React.
- Preview: `import preview from "#/storybook/preview"` (maps to `apps/vue/.storybook`).
- Preview / decorators: `apps/vue/.storybook/`.
- Import components as `@pisagor/vue` (light) or `@pisagor/vue/<heavy>`.
- **Hidden catalog metadata:** same `parameters.metadata` rules as React — required `api` + `taxonomy` on `@pisagor/vue` component stories; typed via [`addonMetadata`](../../../apps/vue/.storybook/addons/metadata-addon.ts). Mirror the React sibling when porting.

## Meta

**Required:** `component`, `title`, `parameters.docs.description.component`. On `@pisagor/react` / `@pisagor/vue` component stories also `parameters.metadata.api` and `parameters.metadata.taxonomy`.

**Do not set on meta:** shared `args`, `argTypes` — Controls infers from component types.

**Compound components:** declare `subcomponents` on meta — map each exported part (`Trigger`, `Content`, `Item`, …).

**Title:** `Components/<Category>/<Component Name>` — use an existing category when possible:

`Actions`, `Data Display`, `Feedback`, `Forms`, `Layout`, `Media`, `Marketing`, `Navigation`, `Overlay`, `Utilities`

Sub-modules may nest under the parent: `Components/Data Display/<Parent>/<Sub Module>`.

**Component description:** one or two plain sentences — what the component does for the user. No prop names, API jargon, or alias lists. A short cross-reference to a sibling component is OK when it prevents confusion (e.g. Menu vs Dropdown Menu).

**Docs (`parameters.docs`):** only user-visible Autodocs copy — typically `description.component`.

**Hidden catalog metadata (`@pisagor/react` / `@pisagor/vue` stories):** set on `parameters.metadata` — not on `tags` or `docs`. These fields are for agents / tooling / MCP and do **not** render in Storybook Docs UI. Typed via `addonMetadata` in each runner preview ([React](../../../apps/react/.storybook/addons/metadata-addon.ts), [Vue](../../../apps/vue/.storybook/addons/metadata-addon.ts)).

```tsx
parameters: {
  docs: {
    description: {
      component: "Draws attention to a short message without blocking the rest of the interface.",
    },
  },
  metadata: {
    aliases: ["banner", "callout"], // optional; kebab-case; omit when none
    api: "compound-shorthand", // closed | compound | compound-shorthand
    taxonomy: "standard", // primitive | standard | pattern
  },
},
```

- **`api`** — required on `@pisagor/react` / `@pisagor/vue` component meta; public API model. Do not repeat in `description.component`.
- **`taxonomy`** — required on `@pisagor/react` / `@pisagor/vue` component meta.
- **`aliases`** — optional alternative names for discovery; single source — do not repeat in `description`.
- Do not reference third-party design systems or libraries in descriptions or aliases.
- Do not add a custom `parameters.docs.page` to surface these fields.

## Tags

Use `tags` only for **status** — not for taxonomy, aliases, or package scope. Category and package live in `title` only (`Components/…`, `Forms/…`, `Recipes/…`).

```tsx
const meta = preview.meta({
  title: "Components/Actions/Button",
  parameters: {
    docs: { description: { component: "…" } },
    metadata: { api: "closed", taxonomy: "primitive" },
  },
});
```

**API (`parameters.metadata.api`, `@pisagor/react` / `@pisagor/vue` components):**

| Value | Meaning |
| --- | ------- |
| `closed` | Single props surface; no subpart composition |
| `compound` | `Foo.Root` + subparts; composition via compound parts |
| `compound-shorthand` | Shorthand default export + `Foo.Root` for advanced composition |

**Taxonomy (`parameters.metadata.taxonomy`, `@pisagor/react` / `@pisagor/vue` components):**

| Value | Meaning |
| --- | ------- |
| `primitive` | Single control or minimal styled element |
| `standard` | One UI concept (may be compound or closed) |
| `pattern` | Multi-component UX orchestration |

**Aliases (`parameters.metadata.aliases`, `@pisagor/react` / `@pisagor/vue` components):**

- Optional; kebab-case strings (`stepper`, `command-palette`, `banner`).
- 0–4 meaningful aliases per component; omit when the canonical name is enough.
- Do not duplicate aliases in `description.component`.

**Status tags (optional):**

| Tag | TSDoc |
| --- | ----- |
| `experimental` | `@beta` on the component export |
| `deprecated` | `@deprecated` on the component export |

**Autodocs:** enabled globally in each runner’s `preview` — do not set per story.

New `@pisagor/react` / `@pisagor/vue` component stories: set `title`, `parameters.metadata.api`, `parameters.metadata.taxonomy`, and `parameters.docs.description.component`; add `aliases` when helpful. `@pisagor/react-form` / `@pisagor/vue-form` stories use `Forms/…` titles; blocks packages use `Blocks/…` titles; recipes use `Recipes/…` titles. Copy a sibling story when unsure.

## File layout

1. **Imports** — `preview`, component(s), icons/helpers.
2. **Meta** — single `preview.meta({ … })` block.
3. **Stories** — exported in [story order](#story-order) below.
4. **Fixtures** — shared sample data at the **bottom** (lowercase const names, e.g. `users`).

## Story order

Skip groups that do not apply.

| Order | Kind | Examples |
| ----- | ---- | -------- |
| 1 | **Default** | `Default` — minimal, standard use; **one instance only** |
| 2 | **Visual variants** | `Sizes`, `Shapes`, `Variants` — one axis per story; grid in one `render` |
| 3 | **Functional states** | `Disabled`, `Loading`, `Fallback`, `Invalid` — one concern per story |
| 4 | **Composition** | `WithIcon`, `Nested`, `Group` — compound usage or integration with other components |
| 5 | **Context** | `Controlled`, `Placements`, `CloseBehavior` — when they teach a real use case |
| 6 | **`Compound`** (compound + shorthand only) | Last story — `Foo.Root` with subparts; shorthand stories come first |

For components with both shorthand and compound APIs, export a final **`Compound`** story that demonstrates `Foo.Root` + subparts. Prefer shorthand in all other stories unless composition flexibility is required (`asChild`, custom markup).

## Default

- **Closed components:** pass props via `args` on the story (not on meta).
- **Compound / overlay components:** use `render` with trigger + content; prefer `Trigger asChild` + `Button`.
- **Omit default props** — do not pass values that match component defaults.
- **One example** — no galleries or compositions in `Default`.

```tsx
export const Default = meta.story({
  args: {
    alt: "Elena Garcia",
    fallback: "EG",
    src: "https://randomuser.me/api/portraits/women/5.jpg",
  },
});
```

## Other stories

- **One story = one idea** — gallery stories vary only the axis being shown.
- **Prefer `args`** for a single instance; **`render`** for layout, hooks, or composition.
- **Do not** add stories for escape-hatch props (`imageProps`, `*Props`) — Controls is enough.
- **Do not** duplicate `Default` or mirror an existing story.
- **Names:** PascalCase.
- **Layout:** side-by-side demos use `gap-2` in flex wrappers (not `gap-4`). Do not add `max-w-*`, `mx-auto w-*`, or similar width constraints on the component under test — stories show components at their natural width (`w-full` where the component defines it).
- **Fixtures:** inline when used once; shared const at file bottom when reused. No trivial render wrappers — use `render: () => …` directly.

## Sample data

- Dummy data only — no real people, GitHub URLs, or personal handles.
- **Avatars:** `https://randomuser.me/api/portraits/{women|men}/{n}.jpg`
- **Emails / URLs:** `@example.com`, `https://example.com/…`
- **Other images:** `https://picsum.photos/seed/{label}/{w}/{h}`

## Overlays

For Dialog, Sheet, Drawer, Popover, Hover Card, etc.:

- `Default` includes an interactive trigger (e.g. `<Dialog.Trigger asChild><Button … /></Dialog.Trigger>`).
- Add stories for close behaviour, scroll, sides, or non-modal only when `Default` does not cover them.
- Use `useState` / controlled `open` when the story is about controlled usage.
